    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d282">

                <pb facs="0364" n="346" sameAs="frus:frus1946v11/pg346"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/6–1546: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Adam</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-06-15T18:00:00-04:00">June 15, 1946—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>331. Representatives AP, UP and Grace have asked us express to you their
                    appreciation your assistance (second paragraph urtel 535 and urtel 533).</p>
                <p>For your confidential information we have recommended to Grace their company
                    immediately dispatch responsible official American citizen to La Paz to take
                    temporary charge and to investigate charges political activity by Grace Bolivian
                    personnel. In latter connection Grace informed that while in absence proof we
                    assumed no political activity their personnel we would view any such activity
                    with extreme disfavor (see Dept press release of December 11, 1945 regarding
                    attitude participation American companies in local political affairs).</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
